ummmm, the castle isn't a hell level (ie. it shouldn't be one).
i'm assuming that you're referring to that sprawling place somewhere
around level 30. The oracle has some advice on the matter but let me
point out that the castle contains within it a wand of wishing. it is
possible to fall thru one of several trapdoors (near the postern)
and land in hell but the recommended way to go to deep hell (assuming,
of course, that you can stand the heat) is use a level teleport trap
while possessing the attribute of teleport control. you can get
teleport control by two means and it should noted that magic
protection, an attribute of certain armors, will prevent you from
activating the trap successfully. level teleport traps are not that
uncommon so you should be able to find one.

okay, you level teleport and request to go to level 99. you probably
won't get there since most 3.0 dungeons only have 50 levels, however
you will go to the deepest level (50). this will be a maze level and
you'll need to find the wizard of yendor's castle on one of these
hell-maze levels. the wizard possesses the amulet of yendor which
you'll need to win the game. get it somehow and start back up. i sent
you to deepest hell because while in hell there are no downstairs,
as you may have guessed, only upstairs. try to eventually escape
the dungeon, be prepared for hidden surprises (since you possess
the powerful amulet) and always consider a final challenge perhaps
lurking around the next bend.

oh yeah, the hell mazes can be strange and Vlad (the Impaler) is
known to live in a tower in the middle of a hell-maze which is only
accessible from its deepest level (i.e. if you miss the opening
you'll have to level teleport back down to get in naturally).

fare thee well ...

